# Non-Heuristic Mandate (ABSOLUTE — EVERY EDIT)

**Summarized chat:** Cursor may compress this thread. If summarized, mid-task, or unsure what rules still apply → **re-read this file** before planning or editing. Summarization does **not** relax this mandate.

Applies to **bugs, features, refactors, perf, and cleanup** — not only lag or planning.

## Before any code change

1. **Canonical owner** — one system/API owns this behavior end-to-end.
2. **6-row audit** (below) — all rows; any fail → redesign or owner-approved ⚠ exception in chat.
3. **Changelog:** `Fix type: non-heuristic fix` (every code fix — owner uses this to spot forgotten mandate) + `How this protects SSOT` + `Heuristics added:` + `Why (not) heuristic:` — vacuous lines = violation.

## 6-row audit

| # | Pass requires |
|---|----------------|
| 1 | Single owner — no parallel owner |
| 2 | One apply path — no second preview/save/commit/hover path |
| 3 | No identity branches — no `if node/tab/scene/skill_id ==` for this behavior |
| 4 | No UI-only state — sim/commit/slots/`GameSettings` see the same truth |
| 5 | Reusable — other skills/screens use same path without new `if` |
| 6 | Obsolete path removed — delete old hack in the **same** change |

## Forbidden without ⚠ exception (any domain)

- Second truth path (preview ≠ commit, hover ≠ slots, range ≠ latest stand)
- Defer/throttle/pending flags on input intent (hover, route, range, preview board)
- `if ability.id == …` when data/`EffectData` can express it
- Refactor that copies logic without deleting the old path
- Feature or fix wired only through presentation flags/meta

**Owner phrase:** “Walk the table” → answer every audit row in plain language.

Detail when editing code: `global-systems-first.mdc` · planning preview: `move-preview-intent-truth.mdc` · range: `action-range-latest-stand.mdc` · perf subordinate: `minimal-performance-impact.mdc`
